live signal to being

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:26.560
able to distribute that live
signal to the end users.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:29.050
And then being able to
help you better monetize,

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:31.710
we are providing
products and solutions

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:34.830
for each of those steps
in your supply chain.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.680
Similarly, we have
products and solutions

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:41.235
for some of the other verticals
inside media and entertainment.

00:06:41.235 --> 00:06:43.110
MARK MANDEL: So what
would that actually look

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.520
like from, say, a
customer point of view?

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.890
Like say, if I'm watching
TV, I may not notice it.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:48.427
But what would
be, say, something

00:06:48.427 --> 00:06:50.760
that might be happening behind
the scenes to a broadcast

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.209
that I might be watching?

00:06:52.209 --> 00:06:54.000
AMIT PANDE: So from a
consumer perspective,

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.090
all the way from, say, there's
a typical Super Bowl game that

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:59.900
is being broadcasted,
we capture that signal

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:03.660
on the broadcaster's
on site premise,

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:06.810
upload it to Google
Cloud, transcode it

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:08.610
in all the different
versions for you

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:12.170
to be able to consume on your
mobile, on your Apple TV,

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:15.180
on your Roku, on your
connected devices,

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.620
and then being
able to distribute

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.437
that through Google's
Cloud Distribution network

00:07:19.437 --> 00:07:21.270
as well as third party
distribution network,

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:23.880
so that you have a seamless
experience when you're

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.884
watching this content online.

00:07:25.884 --> 00:07:26.800
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Cool.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.730
So I've been working lately
with a bunch of Go Meetups

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:31.740
to be able to do
live streaming, which

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:34.030
is like YouTube Live
and stuff like that.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:35.970
So I guess that what
you're talking about

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.070
is basically the same
idea of YouTube Live,

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:39.575
but without having
YouTube involved.

00:07:39.575 --> 00:07:40.950
So like, the whole
infrastructure

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:42.330
is run by Google.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.737
And you can
[INAUDIBLE] anything?

00:07:44.737 --> 00:07:45.820
AMIT PANDE: Yeah, exactly.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:48.600
So it's, in fact, using
the similar infrastructure

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:51.090
as what YouTube is
using, but providing

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:54.570
that as infrastructure as
a service to third party

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:58.770
broadcasters, like all of the
large TV networks out there.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:02.500
And it can be used for
streaming live events.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:06.090
It can be used for just
creating your own live channel

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:09.030
as well as being able to
distribute your video on demand

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:09.960
assets.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.030
FRANCESC CAMPOY: So
maybe the answer is no.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:15.204
But can you talk a little
bit about who is doing this?

00:08:15.204 --> 00:08:17.620
AMIT PANDE: So we have a lot
of large customers out there.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:21.180
For example, we had a
very recent presentation

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.680
at Google Next in New York.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.990
And Univision was
sharing the stage

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:29.340
with us talking about their
journey of moving from on-prem

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:31.620
to Google Cloud infrastructure.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:35.044
And we have a lot more customers
that are using our service.

00:08:35.044 --> 00:08:35.919
MARK MANDEL: Awesome.

00:08:35.919 --> 00:08:39.270
Well, I guess I'm going to ask
maybe the obvious question.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:41.909
We are a company that tends to
be known for machine learning

00:08:41.909 --> 00:08:42.570
