00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:16.810
they're actually moving
the camera itself to be

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:18.409
able to follow that activity.

00:12:18.409 --> 00:12:20.200
So that's an example
where that is actually

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:22.870
happening on the creation side.

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:25.330
You can imagine as
viewers are watching,

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:27.550
they may be like, I
want to be able to view

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:31.630
this particular player's
perspective on the field.

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:33.920
And every person would want
a different one, correct?

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:37.519
Again, machine learning can
help identify as well as

00:12:37.519 --> 00:12:39.310
help you generate that
personalized stream,

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:41.004
so that you can
connect with the users.

00:12:41.004 --> 00:12:42.670
FRANCESC CAMPOY: So
I guess that that is

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:44.590
pretty hard In Real Life, IRL.

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:45.299
AMIT PANDE: Yeah.

00:12:45.299 --> 00:12:46.214
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Cool.

00:12:46.214 --> 00:12:48.490
So out of the things that
you were talking about,

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.590
specifically about
the part where

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.450
you were able to
understand the video

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:55.510
and then create maybe like
highlights or whatever,

00:12:55.510 --> 00:12:58.150
that sounds a lot like
the kind of machine

00:12:58.150 --> 00:13:02.710
learning skills that Vision
Intelligence API has, right?

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:05.980
So I feel like that moves
a little bit into, OK,

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:08.110
so that sounds really fun.

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:09.840
How do I do it as a developer?

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:13.270
What are the different APIs
or the different products

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:15.652
that I can use in order to
create such an experience?

00:13:15.652 --> 00:13:16.360
AMIT PANDE: Yeah.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:19.570
So on the machine
learning side, actually we

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:20.590
have a full spectrum.

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:25.000
We have TensorFlow for you to be
able to build your own models.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:27.490
We also have Google Cloud
Machine Learning Engine,

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.340
which is a managed
end to end service

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:35.170
that you can use to analyze your
data and build your own models.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.720
And then we have
readily available APIs

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:40.860
which are trained
on Google's data

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:44.420
that you can use to integrate
into your application,

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:47.680
so all the way from natural
language understanding APIs

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:50.860
to converting your speech
to text to translating

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:53.830
text and also, most
importantly for media,

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:56.040
understanding your
images and videos.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:58.630
So specifically,
we have two APIs.

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:01.090
One is our Google
Cloud Vision API

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:04.750
that helps you understand
structural entities

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:10.060
inside your images and
Google Cloud Video API, which

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:13.660
helps you take a video,
segment it into shots,

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.850
and detect labels in the shots.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:20.027
That can then be used for things
like search and recommendations

00:14:20.027 --> 00:14:21.610
and, ultimately, for
generating things

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:23.560
like highlights
or driving better

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:25.164
monetization of your content.

00:14:25.164 --> 00:14:26.080
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Nice.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:29.800
For those that are curious,
