00:22:30.890 --> 00:22:34.250
So I was thinking about
how machine learning is

00:22:34.250 --> 00:22:36.050
getting to a point
where it's also

00:22:36.050 --> 00:22:38.350
able to generate new content.

00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:41.390
Like DDReam is a very cool
example, where you give it

00:22:41.390 --> 00:22:43.460
an image, and it creates
something surrealistic,

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:45.520
like super cool ads
and stuff like that.

00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:49.820
Do you think that in, I don't
know, like 10 to 20 years,

00:22:49.820 --> 00:22:52.880
we'll be able to see
videos generated directly

00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:55.220
completely by machine learning?

00:22:55.220 --> 00:22:58.250
AMIT PANDE: I think over time
we will build probably maybe

00:22:58.250 --> 00:22:59.710
in five to seven years.

00:22:59.710 --> 00:23:00.700
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Oh,
wow, five to seven.

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:01.200
Wow.

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:04.820
AMIT PANDE: This is probably
the self-driving car space,

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:07.880
where I think the step
one in that process

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:11.540
is going to use data to assist
with the creative process

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:13.100
of content creation.

00:23:13.100 --> 00:23:15.910
And then over time,
you can imagine.

00:23:15.910 --> 00:23:17.620
Say you have raw
footage of whatever,

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:19.730
30 hours of raw footage.

00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:22.070
A very good example, which
makes us a little [INAUDIBLE]

00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:24.100
is reality TV show, correct?

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:28.554
We have like 10 cameras and
24 by 7 shooting, correct?

00:23:28.554 --> 00:23:29.720
So there's a lot of content.

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:31.460
You need to condense
it down to like

00:23:31.460 --> 00:23:34.040
30 minutes or 40 minutes of
what people are going to watch.

00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:36.980
And there is no perfect answer
of what's right there, correct?

00:23:36.980 --> 00:23:38.870
And you can imagine
machine learning kind

00:23:38.870 --> 00:23:41.540
of combining and learning
from user preferences

00:23:41.540 --> 00:23:43.360
and taste to
actually finding out

00:23:43.360 --> 00:23:45.030
these are the actors
your interested in.

00:23:45.030 --> 00:23:50.210
These are the kind of semantic
moments that appeal to you,

00:23:50.210 --> 00:23:52.180
and using that to
take your raw footage

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:55.490
and summarizing it down to 30
minutes that you're interested.

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:58.460
So that's the extreme
example, correct?

00:23:58.460 --> 00:24:03.020
Obviously, would it be able to
generate this perfect episode

00:24:03.020 --> 00:24:04.690
of "House of Cards? for me?

00:24:04.690 --> 00:24:07.920
I mean, we are definitely
far from that, correct?

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:10.550
But you can start
thinking about applying it

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:13.670
to things like ad creatives,
and then maybe taking

00:24:13.670 --> 00:24:17.559
content where it's already
being stitched together.

00:24:17.559 --> 00:24:19.100
There's a lot of
raw footage that you

00:24:19.100 --> 00:24:20.570
need to condense down to.

00:24:20.570 --> 00:24:22.790
Maybe games is
another example where

00:24:22.790 --> 00:24:26.030
